From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:42:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-paragraph auto base direction and first-strong lookup

parley_engine can force a base direction (BaseDirection::Ltr/Rtl) but
always resolves Auto with a single whole-text first-strong detection.
HTML's unicode-bidi:plaintext (textarea/pre dir=auto) re-runs
first-strong per UAX#9 paragraph.

AnalysisOptions::auto_per_paragraph splits Auto resolution at class-B
separators (CRLF = one separator), resolves each segment on a scratch
resolver, and splices levels back; the first paragraph donates the
layout-wide base_level, which only alignment uses; reordering is per
run.

The parley half of this patch (BaseDirection::AutoPerParagraph on the
builders and PlainEditor) lives in the parley series.

HTML's dir=auto directionality is a DOM-side scan (it excludes bdi/
script/style/textarea subtrees and dir-attributed descendants), which a
text-stream resolver cannot express. The embedder walks text nodes
itself and needs only the per-chunk classification. Classifies via the
same parley_data properties analyze_text uses: strong L is Ltr, strong R
or AL is Rtl, and anything else is None, so the caller keeps walking.

The classifier lives in parley_engine, which owns the parley_data
properties; parley re-exports it as parley::first_strong_direction
(returning parley::BaseDirection) in the parley series.
